448
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:52,880
you're looking at thousands of

449
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:55,160
counterfeit sneakers passing through

450
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:58,000
authentication centers annually, being

451
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:59,640
certified as real, sold at real prices,

452
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:03,640
and delivered to buyers who have no

453
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:05,480
idea. And StockX is just one platform.

454
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:07,720
GOAT has its own authentication

455
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:10,120
pipeline. eBay launched its own

456
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:12,280
authenticity guarantee program. Each of

457
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:14,839
these services catches the vast majority

458
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:16,880
of fakes, but the vast majority is not

459
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:19,800
all of them. And the difference between

460
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:23,000
almost all and all is a gap that real

461
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:26,560
people fall into. People who paid 300,

462
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:28,760
400, $500 for a shoe because a platform

463
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:30,240
they trusted told them it was genuine.

464
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:32,280
This is the part of the counterfeiting

465
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:34,000
economy that nobody thinks about when

466
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:36,320
they picture a guy selling knock-offs

467
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:38,000
out of a van. The buyer in that scenario

468
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:40,280
knows the risk. They're making a

469
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:43,080
conscious decision to pay $40 for

470
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:45,000
something that would normally cost 170,

471
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:47,120
and they understand the trade-off. The

472
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:49,200
buyer on an authenticated platform does

473
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:51,280
